From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rachapalli Bandi Jagadeesh <jagadeesh.rachapalli.bandi@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 23:37:05 +0530
Subject: drm/suballoc: fall through to kernel drm_suballoc.h when helper not built

The copied drm_suballoc.h carries the newer allocator that splits
drm_suballoc_new() into drm_suballoc_alloc() + drm_suballoc_insert().

On kernels that already ship drm_suballoc (e.g. 6.x) the backport does
not build its own drm_suballoc helper (BUILD_XE_DRM_SUBALLOC_HELPER is
only enabled for 5.15/5.16).  In that case the kernel provides everything
except the alloc()/insert() split, which is emulated with static inline
wrappers in backport-include/drm/drm_suballoc.h.

Because the backport include path is searched before the kernel headers,
this copied header shadows the kernel's own <drm/drm_suballoc.h> and
re-declares drm_suballoc_alloc()/drm_suballoc_insert() as non-static
prototypes.  Those collide with the shim's static inline definitions:

error: static declaration of 'drm_suballoc_alloc' follows non-static declaration

Guard the copied allocator behind CPTCFG_BUILD_XE_DRM_SUBALLOC_HELPER.
When the helper is not built, fall through via #include_next to the
kernel's own <drm/drm_suballoc.h> so the shim can supply the alloc()/
insert() split without conflicting prototypes.

Signed-off-by: Rachapalli Bandi Jagadeesh <jagadeesh.rachapalli.bandi@intel.com>
---
 include/drm/drm_suballoc.h | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/drm/drm_suballoc.h b/include/drm/drm_suballoc.h
index 29befdd..c7ed315 100644
--- a/include/drm/drm_suballoc.h
+++ b/include/drm/drm_suballoc.h
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@
  * Copyright © 2022 Intel Corporation
  */
 #ifndef _DRM_SUBALLOC_H_
+
+#ifdef CPTCFG_BUILD_XE_DRM_SUBALLOC_HELPER
 #define _DRM_SUBALLOC_H_
 
 #include <drm/drm_mm.h>
@@ -111,4 +113,8 @@ drm_suballoc_dump_debug_info(struct drm_suballoc_manager *sa_manager,
 
 #endif
 
+#else
+#include_next <drm/drm_suballoc.h>
+#endif /* CPTCFG_BUILD_XE_DRM_SUBALLOC_HELPER */
+
 #endif /* _DRM_SUBALLOC_H_ */
-- 
